ADDRESS: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/E._A._Siddiq
==================================================
Ebrahimali Abubacker Siddiq (15 July 1937 – 22 January 2026) was an Indian agricultural scientist, whose research in  [LINK: (genetics) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Genetics]  and  [LINK: (plant breeding) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Plant_breeding]  is reported to have assisted in the development of various high-yielding rice varieties such as dwarf  [LINK: (basmati) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Basmati]  and hybrid rice. [LINK: ([1]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/E._A._Siddiq#cite_note-ABF-1]  The government of India honoured Siddiq in 2011 with its fourth-highest civilian award,  [LINK: (Padma Shri) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Padma_Shri] . [LINK: ([2]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/E._A._Siddiq#cite_note-Padma_Shri-2]


# BACKGROUND #

E. A. Siddiq was born on 15 July 1937 in  [LINK: (Ilayangudi) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ilaiyangudi] , a town in  [LINK: (Sivaganga District) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sivaganga_district] ,  [LINK: (Madras Province) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Madras_Province] ,  [LINK: (British India) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/British_India] . [LINK: ([3]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/E._A._Siddiq#cite_note-3]  [LINK: ([4]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/E._A._Siddiq#cite_note-4]  His graduate studies were completed in Botany (1959) [LINK: ([5]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/E._A._Siddiq#cite_note-INSA-5]  from the  [LINK: (University of Madras) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/University_of_Madras]  following which he obtained masters (1964) [LINK: ([5]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/E._A._Siddiq#cite_note-INSA-5]  and doctoral degrees (1968) [LINK: ([5]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/E._A._Siddiq#cite_note-INSA-5]  in  [LINK: (Cytogenetics) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cytogenetics] , under the supervision of renowned botanist,  [LINK: (M. S. Swaminathan) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/M._S._Swaminathan] , from the  [LINK: (Indian Agricultural Research Institute) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Indian_Agricultural_Research_Institute]  (IARI). [LINK: ([1]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/E._A._Siddiq#cite_note-ABF-1]  [LINK: ([6]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/E._A._Siddiq#cite_note-CDFD-6]  His career started at his alma mater, the Indian Agricultural Research Institute, as a cytogeneticist in 1968, [LINK: ([1]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/E._A._Siddiq#cite_note-ABF-1]  [LINK: ([6]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/E._A._Siddiq#cite_note-CDFD-6]  [LINK: ([7]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/E._A._Siddiq#cite_note-Padmashree_Prof_Dr_E_A_Siddiq-7]  a post he held till 1976 when he was promoted as the Senior Scientist. [LINK: ([5]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/E._A._Siddiq#cite_note-INSA-5]  [LINK: ([1]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/E._A._Siddiq#cite_note-ABF-1]  [LINK: ([6]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/E._A._Siddiq#cite_note-CDFD-6]  In 1983, he was deputed to Egypt as the Rice Breeder and in 1986, he was transferred to Philippines as the Professor of Genetics. [LINK: ([1]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/E._A._Siddiq#cite_note-ABF-1]  In 1987, he returned to India as the Project Director of the  [LINK: (Directorate of Rice Research) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Directorate_of_Rice_Research] , Hyderabad and worked there till 1994. [LINK: ([5]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/E._A._Siddiq#cite_note-INSA-5]  [LINK: ([1]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/E._A._Siddiq#cite_note-ABF-1]  The next move was to  [LINK: (Indian Council of Agricultural Research) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Indian_Council_of_Agricultural_Research]  (ICAR), New Delhi as the Deputy Director General of the Crop Science Division. [LINK: ([6]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/E._A._Siddiq#cite_note-CDFD-6]

In 1997 Siddiq was honoured as the National Professor of ICAR and in 2002, [LINK: ([1]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/E._A._Siddiq#cite_note-ABF-1]  [LINK: ([7]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/E._A._Siddiq#cite_note-Padmashree_Prof_Dr_E_A_Siddiq-7]  he took charge of the  [LINK: (Centre for DNA Fingerprinting and Diagnostics) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Centre_for_DNA_Fingerprinting_and_Diagnostics]  (CDFD) as the Distinguished Chair. [LINK: ([5]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/E._A._Siddiq#cite_note-INSA-5]  [LINK: ([6]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/E._A._Siddiq#cite_note-CDFD-6]  On his retirement in 2007, he was appointed the Adjunct Scientist at CFFD. [LINK: ([5]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/E._A._Siddiq#cite_note-INSA-5]  He also held the positions of Adjunct Professor of the  [LINK: (University of Hyderabad) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/University_of_Hyderabad] , Adjunct Professor of the Indian Agricultural Research Institute (IARI) and the Honorary Professor of Biotechnology at  [LINK: (Acharya NG Ranga Agricultural University) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Acharya_NG_Ranga_Agricultural_University] , Hyderabad. [LINK: ([5]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/E._A._Siddiq#cite_note-INSA-5]  [LINK: ([1]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/E._A._Siddiq#cite_note-ABF-1]  [LINK: ([6]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/E._A._Siddiq#cite_note-CDFD-6]

Siddiq died on 22 January 2026, at the age of 88. [LINK: ([8]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/E._A._Siddiq#cite_note-8]


# POSITIONS #

Siddiq was a member of the scientific advisory council of the  [LINK: (Prime Minister of India) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Prime_Minister_of_India]  from 2004 to 2009. [LINK: ([1]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/E._A._Siddiq#cite_note-ABF-1]  He sat on the Board of Members of the  [LINK: (International Rice Research Institute) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/International_Rice_Research_Institute]  as well as on the Executive Committee of the Agri Biotech Foundation. [LINK: ([1]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/E._A._Siddiq#cite_note-ABF-1]  He was a member of the working group for the Eleventh Five Year Plan (2007–2012) of India. [LINK: ([9]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/E._A._Siddiq#cite_note-Planning_Commission-9]  He was also a member of the Research Advisory Committee of the National Research Centre on Plant Biotechnology, an Indian Council of Agricultural Research (ICAR) subsidiary. [LINK: ([10]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/E._A._Siddiq#cite_note-NRCPB-10]

Siddiq was the chairman of the Farm and Rural Science Foundation of  [LINK: (The Federation of Andhra Pradesh Chambers of Commerce and Industry) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Federation_of_Andhra_Pradesh_Chambers_of_Commerce_and_Industry] . [LINK: ([11]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/E._A._Siddiq#cite_note-Hybiz_TV-11]  He also served as a council member of National Science academy, India from 1998 till 2000. [LINK: ([5]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/E._A._Siddiq#cite_note-INSA-5]


# LEGACY #

Siddiq is credited with contributions on the scientific, academic and organizational fronts. [LINK: ([6]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/E._A._Siddiq#cite_note-CDFD-6]  His research primarily focussed on genetic research and applied breeding of rice, for improving the yield and quality, and is reported to have assisted in the development of ten high-yielding rice varieties. [LINK: ([5]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/E._A._Siddiq#cite_note-INSA-5]  [LINK: ([6]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/E._A._Siddiq#cite_note-CDFD-6]  A variety of dwarf basmati rice (Pusa Basmati-1), claimed to be the first high-yielding variety in its class, [LINK: ([1]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/E._A._Siddiq#cite_note-ABF-1]  and quick maturing varieties such as Pusa 2-21, Pusa 33, Pusa 4 and Pusa 834 are credited to Siddiq. [LINK: ([6]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/E._A._Siddiq#cite_note-CDFD-6]  [LINK: ([5]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/E._A._Siddiq#cite_note-INSA-5]  His contribution is also reported in the development of DRRH-1, a first-generation Indian hybrid. [LINK: ([6]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/E._A._Siddiq#cite_note-CDFD-6]  [LINK: ([5]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/E._A._Siddiq#cite_note-INSA-5]  Siddiq also did basic research on adaptability, stability and the potential of convergent breeding of various rice breeds. His research also covered the cytogenetic and phylogenetic aspects of rice breeding. [LINK: ([6]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/E._A._Siddiq#cite_note-CDFD-6]

Siddiq was a part of the project for enhancement of rice research in Egypt, under the USAID-funded Rice Breeder programme of  [LINK: (International Rice Research Institute) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/International_Rice_Research_Institute]  (IRRI) in 1987 as well as in the establishment of the  [LINK: (Government of India) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Government_of_India] -sponsored National Rice Research Institute in Vietnam. [LINK: ([6]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/E._A._Siddiq#cite_note-CDFD-6]  [LINK: ([5]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/E._A._Siddiq#cite_note-INSA-5]  Working as a consultant for the  [LINK: (World Bank) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/World_Bank] , he designed the projects for agricultural development in Assam and Bangladesh. [LINK: ([5]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/E._A._Siddiq#cite_note-INSA-5]  He is credited with two scientific studies, one in Egypt and the other in India, in the capacity of the consultant to the  [LINK: (Food and Agriculture Organization) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Food_and_Agriculture_Organization]  (FAO). [LINK: ([6]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/E._A._Siddiq#cite_note-CDFD-6]

On the organizational front, Siddiq collaborated with the World Bank/ [LINK: (FAO) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Food_and_Agriculture_Organization]  as consultant and adviser and prepared many project proposals for programmes in Egypt, Sri Lanka, India, Indonesia and the Philippines. [LINK: ([5]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/E._A._Siddiq#cite_note-INSA-5]  [LINK: ([6]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/E._A._Siddiq#cite_note-CDFD-6]  He also helped in the establishment of rice research institutes in Vietnam and Bangladesh. He was a member of the Task Force on Crop Biotechnology, Monitoring and Evaluation Committee and the National Convenor of the Natural Rice Biotechnology Network during the period from 1990 to 2002. [LINK: ([5]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/E._A._Siddiq#cite_note-INSA-5]  [LINK: ([6]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/E._A._Siddiq#cite_note-CDFD-6]

Siddiq is credited with over 150 research publications, [LINK: ([5]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/E._A._Siddiq#cite_note-INSA-5]  [LINK: ([6]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/E._A._Siddiq#cite_note-CDFD-6]  [LINK: ([12]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/E._A._Siddiq#cite_note-FAO-12]  16 of which have been listed by  [LINK: (Microsoft Academic Search) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Microsoft_Academic_Search]  in their online repository [LINK: ([13]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/E._A._Siddiq#cite_note-Microsoft_Academic_Search-13]  and his research findings have been cited in many books and journals. [LINK: ([14]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/E._A._Siddiq#cite_note-Chemical_Aspects_of_Rice_Grain_Quality-14]  [LINK: ([15]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/E._A._Siddiq#cite_note-Breaking_the_Yield_Barrier-15]   He supervised 35 students in their PhD studies [LINK: ([5]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/E._A._Siddiq#cite_note-INSA-5]  and delivered keynote addresses at many conferences. [LINK: ([11]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/E._A._Siddiq#cite_note-Hybiz_TV-11]  [LINK: ([7]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/E._A._Siddiq#cite_note-Padmashree_Prof_Dr_E_A_Siddiq-7]


# AWARDS AND RECOGNITIONS #

Siddiq received several honours starting with the Hari Om Ashram Trust National Award in 1976. [LINK: ([1]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/E._A._Siddiq#cite_note-ABF-1]  [LINK: ([6]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/E._A._Siddiq#cite_note-CDFD-6]  In 1981, he was awarded the  [LINK: (VASVIK Industrial Research Award) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/VASVIK_Industrial_Research_Award] , [LINK: ([16]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/E._A._Siddiq#cite_note-Vasvik-16]  followed by Amrik Singh Cheema Award in 1988, Silver Jubilee Medal from the  [LINK: (Directorate of Rice Research) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Directorate_of_Rice_Research]  (DRR) in 1990 [LINK: ([6]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/E._A._Siddiq#cite_note-CDFD-6]  [LINK: ([5]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/E._A._Siddiq#cite_note-INSA-5]  and  [LINK: (Om Prakash Bhasin Award) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Om_Prakash_Bhasin_Award]  in 1994. [LINK: ([1]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/E._A._Siddiq#cite_note-ABF-1]  [LINK: ([6]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/E._A._Siddiq#cite_note-CDFD-6]  A year later, in 1995, he received the  [LINK: (Borlaug Award) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Borlaug_Award]  and the  [LINK: (Rafi Ahmed Kidwai Award) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rafi_Ahmed_Kidwai_Award] . [LINK: ([6]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/E._A._Siddiq#cite_note-CDFD-6]  [LINK: ([1]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/E._A._Siddiq#cite_note-ABF-1]  [LINK: ([5]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/E._A._Siddiq#cite_note-INSA-5]  Indian National Science Academy honored Siddiq in 1997 with the Silver Jubilee Medal. [LINK: ([1]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/E._A._Siddiq#cite_note-ABF-1]  [LINK: ([6]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/E._A._Siddiq#cite_note-CDFD-6]  [LINK: ([5]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/E._A._Siddiq#cite_note-INSA-5]  He also received the GP Chatterjee Memorial Lecture Award [LINK: ([5]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/E._A._Siddiq#cite_note-INSA-5]  of the  [LINK: (Indian Science Congress Association) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Indian_Science_Congress_Association]  in 2001, the Agricultural Leadership Award in 2008 [LINK: ([1]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/E._A._Siddiq#cite_note-ABF-1]  and appreciative mementos from the  [LINK: (Government of Tamil Nadu) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Government_of_Tamil_Nadu]  and the  [LINK: (Government of Egypt) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Government_of_Egypt] , [LINK: ([6]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/E._A._Siddiq#cite_note-CDFD-6]  besides receiving the Professor Sundar Lal Hora Medal of INSA, (2011) and B. P. Pal Memorial Award of National Academy of Agricultural Sciences (NAAS) (2011–12). [LINK: ([5]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/E._A._Siddiq#cite_note-INSA-5]  In 2011, the  [LINK: (Government of India) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Government_of_India]  included him in the  [LINK: (Republic day honours) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Indian_honours_system] , listing him for the fourth highest civilian award of  [LINK: (Padma Shri) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Padma_Shri] . [LINK: ([1]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/E._A._Siddiq#cite_note-ABF-1]  [LINK: ([2]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/E._A._Siddiq#cite_note-Padma_Shri-2]

Siddiq was an elected Fellow of the  [LINK: (Indian National Science Academy) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Indian_National_Science_Academy]  (1995), [LINK: ([17]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/E._A._Siddiq#cite_note-17]   [LINK: (National Academy of Sciences (India)) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/National_Academy_of_Sciences,_India] , Allahabad and  [LINK: (National Academy of Agricultural Sciences) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/National_Academy_of_Agricultural_Sciences] , New Delhi. [LINK: ([5]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/E._A._Siddiq#cite_note-INSA-5]


